<!--
  MachineBlocks — concept documentation

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept.UnitsAndGrid
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:concept="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept"
  xmlns:mbcore="com.machineblocks.bml.core"
  xmlns:mbunit="com.machineblocks.bml.unit"
  xmlns:mbt="com.machineblocks.bml.type">

  <name>UnitsAndGrid</name>
  <type>concept:UnitsAndGrid</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to MachineBlocks units and the grid</is>

  <documentation>
    MachineBlocks sizes the world in a unit stack:

    mm → mbu → grid → block geometry

    One mbu (MachineBlocks Unit) is 1.6 mm. The default unit grid is [5, 2]: five mbu per XY grid
    step (8 mm) and two mbu per Z grid step (3.2 mm). A size of [1, 1, 1] is therefore an 8×8×3.2 mm
    plate — not a cube. The XY-to-Z grid ratio is 2.5:1; cube-like blocks need Z ≈ 2.5× the XY grid
    extent (for example [2, 2, 5] → 16×16×16 mm).

    Absolute size along an axis is size × unitGrid[axis] × unitMbu × scale, with XY using
    unitGrid[0] and Z using unitGrid[1].

    The bounding box is defined exclusively by size. Other parameters change visible geometry
    inside that box; they do not redefine the spatial contract.

    Geometry parameters use mbu or grid units. Calibration adjustments (for example baseAdjustment)
    use absolute millimetres and must not scale with the global scale factor.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="concept:GeometryConcepts" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — shape modification inside the bounding box.
    </see>
    <see type="mbunit:MBU" relation="Defines">
      MachineBlocks Unit — 1.6 mm.
    </see>
    <see type="mbunit:GridUnitXY" relation="Defines">
      Default XY grid step in mbu.
    </see>
    <see type="mbunit:GridUnitZ" relation="Defines">
      Default Z grid step in mbu.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:SizeXYZ" relation="Defines">
      Integer grid size — spatial contract of a block.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:NativeBlock" relation="SeeAlso">
      Native parameters including size, unitMbu, unitGrid, scale — SSOT.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
